# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# idlectl -- ignored paths
#
# Scope: build artefacts, editor/OS noise, packaging scratch, generated docs.
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: assistant / agent tooling paths.  Naming them in a
# published file is itself evidence that the toolchain was used, so they live in
# .git/info/exclude, which is local-only and never pushed.
#
# Both halves are enforced mechanically by scripts/check-tracked-paths.sh:
#   * it FAILS if such a path is named in this file, and
#   * it FAILS if such a path is not ignored by *something*
#     (`git check-ignore` does not care which file did it).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Rust / Cargo ----------------------------------------------------------
/target/
**/target/
*.rs.bk
*.orig
*.rej
# Cargo.lock IS committed on purpose: this crate ships a binary and the AUR
# build() runs with --frozen.  Do not add it here.
#
# It is a required file, not generated output.  Every cargo step in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml passes --locked or --frozen so that CI resolves the
# same dependency graph the packager will, which makes a missing Cargo.lock a
# hard CI failure rather than a silent network fetch.  Generate it with
# `cargo generate-lockfile` at the workspace root and commit it.

# --- Coverage / profiling --------------------------------------------------
*.profraw
*.profdata
/coverage/
/lcov.info
tarpaulin-report.*
cobertura.xml
perf.data
perf.data.old
flamegraph.svg

# --- Generated documentation ----------------------------------------------
# Man pages are authored as scdoc in man/*.scd; the roff output is generated at
# build time and must never be committed.
man/*.1
man/*.5
man/*.7
man/*.8
man/*.[1-8].gz
*.roff

# --- Arch packaging scratch ------------------------------------------------
# The PKGBUILD lives in a separate AUR repository, so makepkg is never meant to
# run inside this checkout.  These entries only catch the accident.
/pkg/
/PKGBUILD
/.SRCINFO
*.pkg.tar.zst
*.pkg.tar.xz
*.pkg.tar.gz
*.src.tar.gz
/makepkg.log
/*.log
#
# NOTE on makepkg's src/ directory: it is NOT listed here, on purpose.  `/src/`
# is also where a Rust crate keeps its own source, and ignoring it would
# silently untrack the entire program -- a far worse failure than an accidental
# scratch directory.  Git cannot un-ignore the contents of an ignored
# directory, so there is no pattern that separates the two cases.  The scratch
# case is caught instead by scripts/check-tracked-paths.sh, which fails if a
# tracked path looks like makepkg output (PKGBUILD, .SRCINFO, pkg/, *.pkg.tar.*).

# --- Editor / OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# --- Local environment -----------------------------------------------------
# Never publish a developer's environment: it is the classic carrier for host
# names, addresses and credentials.
.env
.env.*
.envrc
.direnv/
/result
/.cache/
*.tmp
